{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shall not do so.</b> To offer incense to the heavens in any place — but only in the place that He shall choose. Another interpretation — <b>And you shall tear down their altars and destroy their name — you shall not do so.</b> A warning to the one who erases the Name and to the one who displaces a stone from the altar or from the Courtyard (Makkot 22). Said R. Yishmael: would it enter your mind that Israel tears down altars? Rather, do not do like their deeds, lest your sins cause the Temple of your fathers to be destroyed (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:42.101293811Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}